course: dictionary
lesson: 16134
title: Describing colours: whitish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some things are not pure white, but they are very close. The ending -ish means a little bit like something, so whitish means almost white, or pale in colour.
explain: «The sky was a whitish grey before the snow came.» The sky is not bright white and not dark grey. The word whitish tells you it is pale, and grey is mixed in.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «almost white» or «a little bit white». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Whitish is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a whitish flower or a whitish sky.
fact: The ending -ish means a little bit like something, as in greenish, reddish and bluish.
fact: Whitish means almost white, or a little bit white; pale in colour.
fact: Common phrases are "whitish grey" and "a whitish powder".
fact: «Whitish» is not the same as «white»: white is pure, and whitish is a shade that is nearly white.
exercise: «The cat had whitish fur on its paws.» What does whitish mean here? | Very dark | Shiny like glass | Bright red | *Almost white
exercise: Which colour is whitish? | *Pale grey-white, nearly white | Deep purple | Dark black | Bright blue
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes a pale, almost white colour: «The sky was a whitish grey.» | *whitish | was | grey | sky
test: In an experiment, the powder turned out to be whitish. What does that tell you? | *It was pale, almost white | It was pure black | It was made of water | It glowed in the dark
test: «The snow had melted into a whitish slush.» Which words help you know the colour? | *Whitish and pale | Snow and had | Into and a | Melted and slush
exam: Which phrase describes a colour that is almost white? | Very dark brown | Bright orange | Sparkling gold | *whitish grey
